  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U10L-READ-1",
      "title": "The Cooking Class Dinner",
      "text": "My cousin studies in the cooking course of a vocational high school. Last month his class made dinner for the parents. Their teacher is a master of Chinese food, and he never mentions his own awards. That morning the kitchen was awful: the automatic oven stopped working and the fish was not fresh. The students had to alter the menu through a quick meeting. They communicated in short sentences and finished on time. In total, they cooked six dishes for forty people. Classical music played, and cherry blossoms on the tables made the room pretty. Parents surrounded my cousin and asked for his recipes. The teacher told them to get in touch with him by e-mail. My cousin did not show off, but I could see he was proud."
    }
  ],
